# SPA Routing — client-side routes are served by the app shell (app.html) and
# every marketing/legal page by its own static HTML.
#
# ORDER IS PART OF THE CONTRACT (Cloudflare's parser, verified with the real
# pages-dev runtime): a rule with a splat or a placeholder CLOSES the static
# budget, and every rule after it counts as dynamic against a 100-rule cap —
# when the cap is hit the parser discards the rest of the file without failing
# the deploy. Cloudflare's docs state the same ordering requirement ("static
# redirects should appear before dynamic redirects"). This file therefore lists
# every static rule first and the /<lang>/* subtree rows LAST; scripts/check-
# spa-routes.mjs fails the build if a static rule ends up after a dynamic one,
# or if the dynamic count exceeds the platform budget. The file used to put the
# subtree rows in the middle, and the real parser silently dropped the app-route
# block at the end — /settings, /security, /shared, /timeline and /voiceLocal
# answered 404 on Cloudflare while every local check stayed green.

# Landing pages (SEO) — the static marketing HTML is the indexable
# content, served at clean URLs with a 200 rewrite so the canonical
# stays https://bookmarkforgeapp.com/ and /es/. Must precede the SPA
# catch-all below.
/       /landing.html  200

